# What are this endpoint's verdicts? One row per metric measured in the most
# recent run that ran anything for this endpoint: the metric id, the dqv:value
# verdict, the conformance level where the metric carries one (only
# sw:metric:service-description does today), and how long the probe took.
# Also returned, in the SAME result set but distinguishably: any metric that
# run recorded as sw:NotMeasured rather than measured, with the reason it was
# declined (today always "cost-ceiling").
#
# ?endpoint is the input. It is substituted with a NamedNode before execution
# (SEP-0007 substitution, which is why it appears in the SELECT projection:
# pyoxigraph only substitutes projected variables), so it is never
# interpolated into this text. See web/queries/endpoint_content.rq's header
# for the full reasoning; this query reuses it rather than repeating it.
#
# A MEASURED row has ?verdict bound (and, where the graph has them, ?level
# and ?elapsedMs); ?reason is unbound. A DECLINED row has ?reason bound;
# ?verdict, ?level and ?elapsedMs are unbound. A caller must read those as two
# different shapes, never as one: "we chose not to run this metric" and "we
# ran it and got this verdict" are different facts, and the graph is explicit
# about which applies to a given metric on a given run. Collapsing a declined
# row into an ordinary measurement (say, by treating ?reason as if it were a
# verdict) would state a confident value for a metric nobody measured that
# run.
#
# "Most recent run" is decided by the run's activity's prov:generatedAtTime, a
# typed xsd:dateTime, exactly as in endpoint_content.rq, and for the same
# reason: today's run IRIs happen to embed an ISO-8601 instant, so string
# ordering would agree by coincidence, and would silently break the day that
# shape changes.
#
# It is expressed as "no newer run recorded anything (a measurement or a
# decline) for this endpoint" rather than as an ORDER BY ... LIMIT 1 subquery,
# and for the identical reason recorded in endpoint_content.rq's header: the
# value substituted for ?endpoint does not reach inside a subquery's own
# projection, so the subquery would pick the newest run in the whole store and
# then fail to join whenever that run did not happen to touch the endpoint
# being asked about. At 548 endpoints, an endpoint whose probe timed out or
# whose sweep failed in the latest run hits exactly that case, routinely
# rather than rarely. FILTER NOT EXISTS is evaluated against the current
# solution, so ?endpoint stays bound inside it and the comparison stays
# per-endpoint.
#
# The run chosen is the one that recorded ANYTHING for this endpoint, measured
# or declined, not the newest run per individual metric: one sweep either
# measures or declines every metric it applies to a given endpoint in the same
# pass, so an endpoint's measured and declined rows from one run always share
# that run's single prov:Activity. Mixing "most recent per metric" in here
# would let a caller see metric:availability from tonight's run beside
# metric:classes from last week's, two different sweeps' opinions presented as
# one, which is exactly the blended answer endpoint_content.rq's header warns
# against for content samples.

PREFIX dqv: <http://www.w3.org/ns/dqv#>
PREFIX prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#>
PREFIX sw: <urn:sparqlwatch:>

SELECT ?endpoint ?run ?generatedAt ?metric ?verdict ?level ?elapsedMs ?reason
WHERE {
  GRAPH ?run {
    ?activity a prov:Activity ;
              prov:generatedAtTime ?generatedAt .
    {
      ?measurement a dqv:QualityMeasurement ;
                   dqv:computedOn ?endpoint ;
                   dqv:isMeasurementOf ?metric ;
                   dqv:value ?verdict ;
                   prov:wasGeneratedBy ?activity .
      OPTIONAL { ?measurement sw:level ?level }
      OPTIONAL { ?measurement sw:elapsedMs ?elapsedMs }
    }
    UNION
    {
      ?notMeasured a sw:NotMeasured ;
                   sw:notMeasuredOn ?endpoint ;
                   sw:notMeasuredMetric ?metric ;
                   sw:notMeasuredReason ?reason ;
                   prov:wasGeneratedBy ?activity .
    }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    GRAPH ?newerRun {
      {
        ?newerThing dqv:computedOn ?endpoint
      }
      UNION
      {
        ?newerThing sw:notMeasuredOn ?endpoint
      }
      ?newerActivity a prov:Activity ;
                     prov:generatedAtTime ?newerGeneratedAt .
    }
    FILTER (?newerGeneratedAt > ?generatedAt)
  }
}
